<title>USA: Fleet Financial completes consolidation.</title>
<headline>Fleet Financial completes consolidation.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON, Mass. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fleet Financial Group said Friday it completed an 18-month conversion of operations associated with its acquisitions of Shawmut National Corp and several units of National Westminster Bank Plc.</p>
<p>More than 700 computer software systems were converted to Fleet common systems, the company said in a statement, adding 564 branches to the Fleet franchise.</p>
<p>Fleet Chief Financial Officer Eugene McQuade said the integration process resulted in cost savings in excess of $600 million in Fleet's annual operating expenses.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
